{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ratio_bounded_of_stripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ratio_bounded_of_stripGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.lean#L53-L67","doc":"**Bounded ratio of two strip-growth solutions.** If `Φ₁` and `Φ₂` are both comparable to\n`phiBProd b`, their ratio is bounded off `Φ₂`'s zeros: `‖Φ₁ z / Φ₂ z‖ ≤ C₁·C₂`. This is the\nraw-ratio boundedness input the Liouville/boundedness capstone consumes (G5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.instPhiBProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.instPhiBProd","kind":"instance","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.lean#L48-L51","doc":"**`phiBProd` is a strip-growth instance** (`C = 1`) — the class is non-vacuous, realized\nby the canonical product itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.comparable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.comparable","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.lean#L40-L46","doc":"**Strip-growth characterization class.** `Φ` is comparable in modulus to the canonical\nproduct `phiBProd b`: some `C > 0` bounds each by `C` times the other, everywhere. This is\nthe growth condition that singles out the physical `Φ_b` among the shift-solutions; it\ncarries the comparability **hypothesis**, not the uniqueness conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}